### Convergence Issues and Outliers  

Convergence problems were generally rare. The main exception was UPI, which showed reduced convergence under moderate sample size, low reliability, and uniform latent predictors. In this scenario, convergence rates were `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("UPI", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "convergence"), 2)`% with the full model and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("UPI", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "convergence"), 2)`% with the linear model. LMS and QML converged well in general, with the lowest rates in the same setting being `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LMS", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "convergence"), 2)`% and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("QML", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "convergence"), 2)`% (full model), and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LMS", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "convergence"), 2)`% and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("QML", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "convergence"), 2)`% (linear model), respectively. LSAM consistently converged, with rates of `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LSAM", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "convergence"), 2)`% across all conditions.

Outlier rates followed a comparable pattern. The most pronounced rates again occurred under moderate sample size, low reliability, and uniform latent predictors. UPI produced the highest outlier frequencies, reaching `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("UPI", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "outlier"), 2)`% with the full model and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("UPI", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "outlier"), 2)`% with the linear model. For the same condition, LSAM also yielded the most outliers (`r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LSAM", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Linear", "outlier"), 2)`% with the linear model and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LSAM", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "outlier"), 2)`% with the full model). In contrast, LMS and QML generated virtually none, with their highest rates reaching only `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("LMS", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "outlier"), 2)`% and `r round(get_convergence_outlier_rate_study_1("QML", "uniform", 400, 0.4, "Full", "outlier"), 2)`% (both full model) in the same scenario as the other approaches. Detailed results for convergence and outliers are provided in Appendix C (see Table C1).


